# Git's text/binary autodetection is a heuristic. Vendored assets are checked in
# byte-for-byte and must never get line-ending conversion — a mangled .bcmap or
# .woff2 fails at runtime in ways that are painful to trace back to git.
*.bcmap  binary
*.woff2  binary
*.pfb    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.webp   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.m4a    binary
*.apk    binary
*.aab    binary
*.jks    binary
*.keystore binary

# Minified vendor code: keep it exactly as published upstream.
vendor/**  -text
